{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2QDimTranspose"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeTwistData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeTwistData","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L181-L195","doc":"**The Hecke twist `θ_λ = q^{c(λ)}` realizes `ModularTwistData`** on any conjugate-closed set `P`\nof weakly-decreasing blocks.  `theta_conj` is discharged by `theta_conjugate` (`θ_{λ'} = θ_λ⁻¹` from\nthe content flip).  Mirrors `heckeVerlindeData`, but needs **no** `1 < q` hypothesis — the twist is\nthe algebraic half of the modular data.  Given the (owner-gated) category identification, this is the\n`T`-matrix of the keystone MTC, alongside `heckeVerlindeData`'s `S`-matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.theta_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.theta_conj","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L179-L179","doc":"**The twist's chirality law** `θ_{λ′} = θ_λ⁻¹` (the `C2`-analogue for the `T`-matrix). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.theta","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L177-L177","doc":"The ribbon twist / modular `T`-matrix eigenvalue `θ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.conj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.conj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L175-L175","doc":"Blocks closed under transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.conj","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The transpose involution `λ ↦ λ′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.parts","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L171-L171","doc":"The finite set of Hecke partition blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.Part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.Part","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Partition index for the Hecke block `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L167-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ModularTwistData","kind":"structure","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L162-L179","doc":"**Modular `T`-matrix / ribbon-twist data** of the keystone modular category — the *second* piece\nof modular data, complementing `VerlindeModularData`'s vacuum `S`-matrix row.  Carries the simple\nobjects (Hecke blocks), the transpose involution, and the diagonal twist `theta` with its chirality\nlaw `theta (λ') = theta(λ)⁻¹`.  Generic `GroupWithZero` (the twist is purely multiplicative — no\npositivity / `ℝ` needed, unlike the `S`-matrix side). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_row","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L155-L158","doc":"The twist on the one-row rep `[n]`, exponent made explicit: `θ_{[n]} = q^{Σ_{j<n} j} = q^{\\binom n2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.two_mul_contentSum_single_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.two_mul_contentSum_single_row","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**The one-row (trivial / symmetric) rep has content sum `\\binom{n}{2}`**: `2·c([n]) = n(n−1)`, the\ntriangular number (`two_mul_sum_range_int`).  So its framing anomaly is `θ_{[n]} = q^{\\binom n2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_single_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_single_row","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L139-L147","doc":"The content sum of the one-row shape `[n]` is `Σ_{j<n} j` (its cells are `(0,0),…,(0,n−1)` with\ncontent `j − 0 = j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_nil","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L133-L135","doc":"**The twist is trivial on the vacuum**: `θ_∅ = 1` (`c(∅) = 0`, the empty diagram has no cells). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**The twist's chirality / bar-parity law (the `C2`-analogue for the `T`-matrix): `θ_{λ'} = θ_λ⁻¹`.**\nThe transpose negates the content sum (`contentSum_conjugate`), and `q^{−c(λ)} = (q^{c(λ)})⁻¹`\n(`zpow_neg`, valid in any `GroupWithZero`).  Complements the `S`-matrix's `qDim_conj`\n(`d_q(λ') = d_q(λ)`): the `S`-datum is transpose-INVARIANT, the `T`-datum transpose-INVERTS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L118-L122","doc":"**The ribbon twist / modular `T`-matrix eigenvalue on the simple `V_λ`**: `θ_λ = q^{c(λ)}`, the\ntopological framing anomaly, with exponent the content sum `c(λ) = Σ_{(i,j)∈λ}(j−i)` (the\nquadratic-Casimir eigenvalue).  A `zpow` (the exponent is a possibly-negative `ℤ`), over a generic\n`GroupWithZero` (§7c — purely algebraic, no `ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L108-L112","doc":"**`C2` on the canonical `Partition.conjugate`.**  Bridge `contentSum_conj` (stated on the merged\n`conj`) to the `QPartitionCombinatorics` conjugate via `conjugate_eq_conj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conj","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L93-L106","doc":"**`C2` for the signed content sum (Σ-level): `c(λ') = − c(λ)`.**  Content negates under transpose\n(`cellContent_transpose_neg`: `c(r,c) = − c(c,r)`); the two column forms above index the *same* cell\nset, so the sum negates.  This is the signed companion of the corpus's `sumSqContents_conj` (squared,\ninvariant), and the general statement behind the single `conjugate_two_content_flip` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conj_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_conj_col","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L82-L91","doc":"**Column form of `contentSum (conj l)`**: rows of the merged conjugate `conj l` are the column\nlengths `colLen l r` (`conj_getD` / `conj_length`), so its cell double sum is the column-indexed one\nover `l`'s diagram — with cell `(r,c)` carrying content `c(r,c) = c − r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_col","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Column form of `contentSum`** (via `cell_fubini`): the row-indexed cell sum equals the\ncolumn-indexed one, `Σ_i Σ_{j<λ_i} c(i,j) = Σ_j Σ_{i<colLen j} c(i,j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_eq_finset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_eq_finset","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**`contentSum` as a `Finset` double sum.**  Unfold the nested `foldl` into the row×column cell\ndouble sum `Σ_i Σ_{j<λ_i} c(i,j)`, matching the shape `cell_fubini` transposes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.foldl_add_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.foldl_add_range","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneModularTwist.lean#L56-L64","doc":"A multiplicative-analogue-free additive `foldl` over `range n` is the `Finset.sum` (the additive\ntwin of `KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.foldl_mul_range`; used to unfold `contentSum`'s nested `foldl`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}